<title>USA: Delgratia trade remains suspended-Nasdaq.</title>
<headline>Delgratia trade remains suspended-Nasdaq.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in Delgratia Mining Corp will remain suspended until a decision has been reached by the Nasdaq Listing Qualifications Panel, the electronic stock market said Monday.</p>
<p>Nasdaq halted trade in the stock at 0903 ET/1303 GMT. The stock was priced at $12 at the time of the halt.  </p>
<p>Delgratia officials have been asked to appear at a hearing before the Nasdaq panel on Wednesday, May 21, Nasdaq said.</p>
<p>Earlier today, Delgratia, on the basis of a letter received from an independent auditor, said there was evidence of tampering with core samples from their Nevada property and that there were insignificant amounts of gold in the deposit.</p>
<p>Delgratia is based British Columbia, Vancouver.</p>
</text>
